Per metre length, taking moments about the downstream toe:

- Dam weight resisting moment:  
  \[
  M_R \approx 32{,}084.9\ \text{kN}\cdot\text{m/m}
  \]

- Water overturning moment:  
  \[
  M_w=\frac{\gamma_w h^3}{6}
  =\frac{9.81(22.6)^3}{6}
  \approx 18{,}873.1\ \text{kN}\cdot\text{m/m}
  \]

- Uplift overturning moment:  
  \[
  M_u=\frac{f_u\gamma_w h B^2}{3}
  =\frac{0.79(9.81)(22.6)(10.7)^2}{3}
  \approx 6{,}684.2\ \text{kN}\cdot\text{m/m}
  \]

- Total overturning moment:
  \[
  M_O=18{,}873.1+6{,}684.2
  =25{,}557.3\ \text{kN}\cdot\text{m/m}
  \]

- Factor of safety:
  \[
  FS_{\text{overturning}}
  =\frac{M_R}{M_O}
  =\frac{32{,}084.9}{25{,}557.3}
  \approx 1.255
  \]

\[
1.255 < 1.50
\]

Therefore the design **does not satisfy** the stated acceptance criterion and **cannot be approved under the given inputs**.

